{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-8955-1",
  "summary": "nginx vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that nginx incorrectly handled certain configurations\nusing the alias directive together with rewrite rules. A remote attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to cause nginx to crash, resulting in a\ndenial of service, or execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2026-15176)\n\nIt was discovered that nginx incorrectly handled map directives using\nregex matching under certain circumstances. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause nginx to crash, resulting in a denial\nof service, or execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2026-93479)\n\nIt was discovered that nginx incorrectly handled HTTP/3 requests when\nproxy_request_buffering was enabled. This issue only affected\nUbuntu 26.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.10. A remote attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to inject data into proxied requests.\n(CVE-2026-95101)\n\nIt was discovered that nginx incorrectly handled asynchronous file I/O\nin certain configurations with Server Side Includes pages. A remote\nattacker could possibly use this issue to cause nginx to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service, or execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2026-97205)\n\nIt was discovered that nginx incorrectly handled SSL session ticket keys\nwhen configured with a shared session cache but without explicit ticket\nkey rotation. This issue only affected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS,\nand Ubuntu 26.10. A remote attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to forge client SSL sessions and bypass\nclient certificate verification.\n(CVE-2026-97629)",
